  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem3F Heckler had Stern Scolding in hand, which counters creature spells with power or toughness 2 or less. Fallaji Archaeologist is a 0/3, so its toughness of 3 makes it ineligible for Stern Scolding. However, Snapback could have been used to bounce the Archaeologist, though spending 2 mana or exiling a blue card to bounce a 0/3 is low value. Actually, re-reading Stern Scolding: it counters creatures with power or toughness 2 or less. The Archaeologist has power 0 (which is ≤ 2), so it IS a valid target for Stern Scolding. Gem3F chose to let it resolve rather than counter it. Fallaji Archaeologist provides card selection (mill 3, potentially draw a noncreature nonland) and a 0/3 or 1/4 body. Using Stern Scolding here would be a 1-for-1 trade preventing the opponent from getting value from the ETB trigger. However, Gem3F has Goblin Charbelcher as their main win condition and may want to hold Stern Scolding for a more threatening creature like Psychic Frog (which is already on the battlefield though). Given that the opponent already has Psychic Frog down and Stern Scolding's best targets are likely already past, spending it on the Archaeologist to deny the ETB value and a blocker seems reasonable. Still, holding countermagic for unknown future threats is defensible.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to counter Fallaji Archaeologist with Stern Scolding, allowing it to resolve and get its ETB mill/card selection trigger.",
      "better_line": "Cast Stern Scolding targeting Fallaji Archaeologist (power 0 ≤ 2, valid target) to deny the ETB card selection and prevent the opponent from developing their board. The best Stern Scolding targets (small creatures like Psychic Frog) may already be on board.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 91,
      "player": "Gem3F Heckler",
      "decision_index": 59,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Casting a second Psychic Frog before combat when the first Psychic Frog could attack. While the opponent has no mana available for interaction, standard sequencing would attack first to avoid giving unnecessary information, then cast the second frog post-combat.",
      "action_taken": "Cast second Psychic Frog in precombat main phase",
      "better_line": "Attack with existing Psychic Frog first (potentially pumping with discards to get past the 0/3 Archaeologist and draw a card), then cast the second Psychic Frog in the second main phase",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 99,
      "player": "Kimi25 Diplom",
      "decision_index": 67,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Failed to discard Street Wraith to Psychic Frog before combat. Street Wraith is essentially a free discard since its main value is cycling (which costs 2 life). Discarding it to Frog pre-combat gives +1/+1 counter for extra damage, and the Frog's combat damage trigger still draws a card. This is strictly better than holding Street Wraith.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority and moved to combat without pumping Psychic Frog",
      "better_line": "Activate Psychic Frog by discarding Street Wraith to put a +1/+1 counter on it, then attack with a 2/3 Frog instead of 1/2, dealing 1 extra damage while still drawing from combat damage",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 100,
      "player": "Kimi25 Diplom",
      "decision_index": 67,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With zero lands on the battlefield, Whir of Invention (XUUU cost) is essentially uncastable this game, while Fallaji Archaeologist (1U) could realistically be cast if even one or two lands are drawn and provides a blocker against the lethal Psychic Frog threats.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Fallaji Archaeologist",
      "better_line": "Discard Whir of Invention, as it requires far more mana to be useful and is the most dead card with zero lands in play. Fallaji Archaeologist is a cheap blocker and card selection tool that could stabilize the board.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 250,
      "player": "Gem3F Heckler",
      "decision_index": 136,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Gem3F Heckler had Snapback available (castable by exiling a blue card from hand - they had multiple blue cards like Disrupting Shoal, Stern Scolding, Spell Snare) and could have bounced the 4/4 Death's Shadow before blockers, saving 4 damage and preventing it from connecting. Instead they only blocked with creatures and took 5 damage, dropping to 8 life instead of potentially 8-9 with much better board position.",
      "action_taken": "Did not cast Snapback and only used creature blockers, taking 5 damage from the attack.",
      "better_line": "Cast Snapback by exiling a blue card (e.g., a Disrupting Shoal) to bounce Death's Shadow, then block both Psychic Frogs with Fallaji Archaeologist and Thundertrap Trainer, taking only 1 damage from Moonshadow and going to 12 life instead of 8.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 344,
      "player": "Gem3F Heckler",
      "decision_index": 158,
    }
